{"abstract":"Molecular understanding of the solid-liquid interface is challenging but essential to elucidate the role of the environment on the kinetics of electrochemical reactions. Alkali metal cations (M+), as a vital component at the interface, are found to be necessary for the initiation of carbon dioxide reduction reaction (CO2RR) on coinage metals, and the activity and selectivity of CO2RR could be further enhanced with the cation changing from Li+ to Cs+, while the underlying mechanisms are not well understood. Herein, using ab initio molecular dynamics simulations with explicit solvation and enhanced sampling methods, we systematically investigate the role of M+ in CO2RR on Cu surface. A monotonically decreasing CO2 activation barrier is obtained from Li+ to Cs+, which is attributed to the different coordination abilities of M+ with *CO2. Furthermore, we show that the competing hydrogen evolution reaction must be considered simultaneously to understand the crucial role of alkali metal cations in CO2RR on Cu surfaces, where H+ is repelled from the interface and constrained by M+. Our results provide significant insights into the design of electrochemical environments and highlight the importance of explicitly including the solvation and competing reactions in theoretical simulations of CO2RR.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Zhang, Zhichao","Li, Hengyu","Shao, Yangfan","Gan, Lin","Kang, Feiyu","Duan, Wenhui","Hansen, Heine Anton","Li, Jia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718755"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Kang, Feiyu","Li, Jia"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Tsinghua University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"molecular understanding of the critical role of alkali metal cations in initiating co sub 000000000002 sub electroreduction on cu 000000000100 surface","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-44896-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718755","identifier":[{"id":"85182656908","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10799043","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38242907","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-d7aad10f-d72d-4378-a0e4-f70739f52644"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CC81C2B6D5332A22A30B7DF173347775"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-44896-x","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/349945177/s41467-024-44896-x.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"tsinghua university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tsinghua University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Energy Conversion and Storage","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Energy Conversion and Storage, Atomic Scale Materials Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhichao","key":"zhangzhichaopau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Zhichao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hengyu","key":"lihengyupau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Hengyu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yangfan","key":"shaoyangfanpau","last":"Shao","name":"Shao, Yangfan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lin","key":"ganlinpau","last":"Gan","name":"Gan, Lin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Feiyu","key":"kangfeiyupau","last":"Kang","name":"Kang, Feiyu","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenhui","key":"duanwenhuipau","last":"Duan","name":"Duan, Wenhui","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Heine Anton","key":"hansenheineantonpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"58a77c80-83b9-4159-8b4c-82fe4fe2b581","name":"Hansen, Heine Anton","orcid":"0000-0001-7551-9470","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jia","key":"lijiapau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Jia","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38242907"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-024-44896-x","issn":["20411723"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"612","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85182656908"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d7aad10f-d72d-4378-a0e4-f70739f52644"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Molecular understanding of the critical role of alkali metal cations in initiating CO<sub>2</sub> electroreduction on Cu(100) surface","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718755","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"As the genome is organized into a three-dimensional structure in intracellular space, epigenomic information also has a complex spatial arrangement. However, most epigenetic studies describe locations of methylation marks, chromatin accessibility regions, and histone modifications in the horizontal dimension. Proper spatial epigenomic information has rarely been obtained. In this study, we designed spatial chromatin accessibility sequencing (SCA-seq) to resolve the genome conformation by capturing the epigenetic information in single-molecular resolution while simultaneously resolving the genome conformation. Using SCA-seq, we are able to examine the spatial interaction of chromatin accessibility (e.g. enhancer-promoter contacts), CpG island methylation, and spatial insulating functions of the CCCTC-binding factor. We demonstrate that SCA-seq paves the way to explore the mechanism of epigenetic interactions and extends our knowledge in 3D packaging of DNA in the nucleus.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Xie, Yeming","Ruan, Fengying","Li, Yaning","Luo, Meng","Zhang, Chen","Chen, Zhichao","Xie, Zhe","Weng, Zhe","Chen, Weitian","Chen, Wenfang","Fang, Yitong","Sun, Yuxin","Guo, Mei","Wang, Juan","Xu, Shouping","Wang, Hongqi","Tang, Chong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-720654"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","Harbin Medical University","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["3D genome","Chromatin accessibility","Chromosomes","DNA methylation","Gene expression","Hi C","Human"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"spatial chromatin accessibility sequencing resolves high order spatial interactions of epigenomic markers","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.87868","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-720654","identifier":[{"id":"38236718","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10945591","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-70b4464d-e326-4b30-af68-8ebec26aed2b"],"keyword":["3D genome","DNA methylation","GpC methyltransferase","Hi-C","chromatin accessibility","chromosomes","gene expression","human","pore-C"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-79188CADEFA3E346C369278E223BD233"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/381060809/elife_87868_v1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.87868","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"bgi","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Cell Biology and Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"harbin medical university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Harbin Medical University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Yeming","key":"xieyemingpau","last":"Xie","name":"Xie, Yeming","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Fengying","key":"ruanfengyingpau","last":"Ruan","name":"Ruan, Fengying","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yaning","key":"liyaningpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yaning","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Meng","key":"luomengpau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Meng","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chen","key":"zhangchenpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Chen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Zhichao","key":"chenzhichaopau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Zhichao","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Zhe","key":"xiezhepau","last":"Xie","locid":"4d117987-83da-492f-a318-536c9a9815fd","name":"Xie, Zhe","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Zhe","key":"wengzhepau","last":"Weng","name":"Weng, Zhe","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Weitian","key":"chenweitianpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Weitian","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Wenfang","key":"chenwenfangpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Wenfang","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yitong","key":"fangyitongpau","last":"Fang","name":"Fang, Yitong","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yuxin","key":"sunyuxinpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Yuxin","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mei","key":"guomeipau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Mei","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Juan","key":"wangjuanpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Juan","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Shouping","key":"xushoupingpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Shouping","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hongqi","key":"wanghongqipau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Hongqi","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chong","key":"tangchongpau","last":"Tang","name":"Tang, Chong","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38236718"],"pub":{"doi":"10.7554/elife.87868","issn":["2050084X"],"journal":"eLife","paperid":"RP87868","status":"p","title":"eLife","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85177826809"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-70b4464d-e326-4b30-af68-8ebec26aed2b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Spatial chromatin accessibility sequencing resolves high-order spatial interactions of epigenomic markers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-720654","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Epigenetic modifications of histones are associated with development and pathogenesis of disease. Existing approaches cannot provide insights into long-range interactions and represent the average chromatin state. Here we describe BIND&MODIFY, a method using long-read sequencing for profiling histone modifications and transcription factors on individual DNA fibers. We use recombinant fused protein A-M.EcoGII to tether methyltransferase M.EcoGII to protein binding sites to label neighboring regions by methylation. Aggregated BIND&MODIFY signal matches bulk ChIP-seq and CUT&TAG. BIND&MODIFY can simultaneously measure histone modification status, transcription factor binding, and CpG 5mC methylation at single-molecule resolution and also quantifies correlation between local and distal elements.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Weng, Zhe","Ruan, Fengying","Chen, Weitian","Chen, Zhichao","Xie, Yeming","Luo, Meng","Xie, Zhe","Zhang, Chen","Wang, Juan","Sun, Yuxin","Fang, Yitong","Guo, Mei","Tan, Chen","Chen, Wenfang","Tong, Yiqin","Li, Yaning","Wang, Hongqi","Tang, Chong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-409341"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["CTCF","CpG methylation","Epigenetics","H3K27me3","Histone modification","Methyltransferase","mA"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bind amp modify a long range method for single molecule mapping of chromatin modifications in eukaryotes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13059-023-02896-y","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-409341","identifier":[{"id":"85151173500","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10052867","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36991510","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1a9dae7c-442c-4007-a19c-4793fad86b26"],"keyword":["CTCF","CpG methylation","Epigenetics","H3K27me3","Histone modification","Methyltransferase","mA"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-F6CDBF608377B9F70F52B94E5D9EB8CB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13059-023-02896-y","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/341880703/s13059_023_02896_y.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"bgi","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Cell Biology and Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Zhe","key":"wengzhepau","last":"Weng","name":"Weng, Zhe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Fengying","key":"ruanfengyingpau","last":"Ruan","name":"Ruan, Fengying","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Weitian","key":"chenweitianpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Weitian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Zhichao","key":"chenzhichaopau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Zhichao","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yeming","key":"xieyemingpau","last":"Xie","name":"Xie, Yeming","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Meng","key":"luomengpau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Meng","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Zhe","key":"xiezhepau","last":"Xie","locid":"4d117987-83da-492f-a318-536c9a9815fd","name":"Xie, Zhe","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chen","key":"zhangchenpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Chen","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Juan","key":"wangjuanpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Juan","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yuxin","key":"sunyuxinpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Yuxin","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yitong","key":"fangyitongpau","last":"Fang","name":"Fang, Yitong","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mei","key":"guomeipau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Mei","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chen","key":"tanchenpau","last":"Tan","name":"Tan, Chen","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Wenfang","key":"chenwenfangpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Wenfang","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yiqin","key":"tongyiqinpau","last":"Tong","name":"Tong, Yiqin","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yaning","key":"liyaningpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yaning","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hongqi","key":"wanghongqipau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Hongqi","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chong","key":"tangchongpau","last":"Tang","name":"Tang, Chong","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36991510"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-023-02896-y","issn":["14747596","1474760X"],"issn_org":["14747596"],"issue":"1","journal":"Genome Biology","paperid":"61","status":"p","title":"Genome Biology","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85151173500"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1a9dae7c-442c-4007-a19c-4793fad86b26"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"BIND&amp;MODIFY : a long-range method for single-molecule mapping of chromatin modifications in eukaryotes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-409341","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Understory vegetation contributes considerably to biodiversity and total aboveground biomass of forest ecosystems. Whereas field inventories and LiDAR data are generally used to estimate understory vegetation density, methods for large-scale and spatially continuous estimation of understory vegetation density are still lacking. For an evergreen coniferous forest area in southern China, we developed and tested an effective and practical remote sensing-driven approach for mapping understory vegetation, based on phenological differences between over and understory vegetation. Specifically, we used plant area volume density (PAVD) calculations based on GEDI data to train a support vector regression model and subsequently estimated the understory vegetation density from Sentinel-2 derived metrics. We produced maps of PAVD for the growing and non-growing season respectively, both performing well compared against independent GEDI samples (R2 = 0.89 and 0.93, p < 0.01). Understory vegetation density was derived from the differences in PAVD between the growing and non-growing season. The understory vegetation density map was validated against field samples from 86 plots showing an overall R2 of 0.52 (p < 0.01), rRMSE = 21%. Our study developed a tangible approach to map spatially continuous understory vegetation density with the combination of GEDI LiDAR data and Sentinel-2 imagery, showing the potential to improve the estimation of terrestrial carbon storage and better understand forest ecosystem processes across larger areas.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Xi, Yanbiao","Tian, Qingjiu","Zhang, Wenmin","Zhang, Zhichao","Tong, Xiaoye","Brandt, Martin","Fensholt, Rasmus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-433864"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nanjing University"],"keyword":["Support vector regression","Understory vegetation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quantifying understory vegetation density using multi temporal sentinel 000000000002 and gedi lidar data","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/15481603.2022.2148338","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-433864","identifier":[{"id":"85142352837","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000889610500001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-43b78bcb-385c-43e3-a01f-8eeab7730a2e"],"keyword":["GEDI LiDAR data","Understory vegetation","plant area volume density","support vector regression"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A815E3614347838EB8DDE2FF0DDF31AD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/15481603.2022.2148338","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/328427337/Quantifying_understory_vegetation_density_using.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Geography"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"nanjing university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Yanbiao","key":"xiyanbiaopau","last":"Xi","locid":"301b35f0-3c61-41f9-a1b4-971a4c28f817","name":"Xi, Yanbiao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Qingjiu","key":"tianqingjiupau","last":"Tian","name":"Tian, Qingjiu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Wenmin","key":"zhangwenminpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"f3774840-2020-41b2-a27c-c1cdf55d58f5","name":"Zhang, Wenmin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Zhichao","key":"zhangzhichaopau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Zhichao","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiaoye","key":"tongxiaoyepau","last":"Tong","locid":"f763c8d5-da73-4b01-9703-1af5e5481d6b","name":"Tong, Xiaoye","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin","key":"brandtmartinpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"ff0528eb-4f80-444b-a7ad-2d2307f7bdc9","name":"Brandt, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-9531-1239","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus","key":"fensholtrasmuspau","last":"Fensholt","locid":"26fbbb5c-3853-4be9-8cab-3dce86446363","name":"Fensholt, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0003-3067-4527","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/15481603.2022.2148338","issn":["15481603"],"issue":"1","journal":"GIScience and Remote Sensing","pages":"2068-2083","status":"p","title":"GIScience and Remote Sensing","volume":"59"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85142352837"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-43b78bcb-385c-43e3-a01f-8eeab7730a2e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Quantifying understory vegetation density using multi-temporal Sentinel-2 and GEDI LiDAR data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-433864","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Due to the n-pulse commutation, the power harmonic distortions caused by power inverters usually concentrate on particular (nk +- m)-order harmonic frequencies. The conventional repetitive control (RC) uses an identical gain to equally compensate for the distortions at all harmonic frequencies. This leads to slow dynamics as it fails to optimize the convergence rate of the RC at dominant harmonic frequencies. The selective harmonic RC (SHRC) can efficiently suppress dominant power harmonic distortions. However, the ratio of the sampling rate of the SHRC to the fundamental frequency must be an integer. This severely limits the use and lowers the performance of the SHRC with a fixed sampling rate in the presence of frequency variations of interested harmonics. To address this problem, this paper proposes a frequency adaptive virtual variable sampling-based SHRC (FA-VVSSHRC) scheme that is immune to the issue of the fractional ratio of the sampling rate to the interested harmonics. The proposed FA-VVS-SHRC scheme can provide flexible fractional phase lead compensation to achieve accurate power harmonic control in the presence of frequency variations. Moreover, it is a low-cost and easy-to-implement solution that does not require hardware modifications. Experiments on a three-phase power inverter and comparison studies are presented to verify its effectiveness.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Liu, Zhichao","Zhou, Keliang","Yang, Yongheng","Wang, Jingcheng","Zhang, Bin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-102292"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Zhang, Bin"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Shanghai Jiao Tong University","University of South Carolina","Wuhan University of Technology"],"keyword":["DC AC inverter","Repetitive control","frequency fluctuation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"frequency adaptive virtual variable sampling based selective harmonic repetitive control of power inverters","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/378223316/20_TIE_1457.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-102292","identifier":[{"id":"85107026413","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b3e4f61c-2a73-4786-bd71-3939c6ac3b16"],"keyword":["DC/AC inverter","frequency fluctuation","repetitive control","selective harmonics","virtual variable sampling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CC6706D310E62FA54F3964A6AB62A660"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/378223316/20_TIE_1457.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of south carolina","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of South Carolina","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"wuhan university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Wuhan University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronics System Integration and Materials"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"shanghai jiao tong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhichao","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Zhichao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Keliang","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Keliang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Y.","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","locid":"d4e88c1b-191c-43c1-90e4-13e51951780e","name":"Yang, Yongheng","name_org":"Yang, Y.","orcid":"0000-0002-1488-4762","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jingcheng","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Jingcheng","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bin","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Bin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tie.2020.3031452","issn":["02780046","15579948"],"issn_org":["02780046"],"issue":"11","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Industrial Electronics","pages":"11339-11347","paperid":"9239879","publisher":"IEEE Industrial Electronics Society","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Industrial Electronics","volume":"68"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85107026413"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b3e4f61c-2a73-4786-bd71-3939c6ac3b16"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Frequency Adaptive Virtual Variable Sampling-based Selective Harmonic Repetitive Control of Power Inverters","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-102292","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Fossil life in the Precambrian is commonly preserved as carbonaceous compressions, where Pre-Cryogenian carbonaceous compressions mainly occur in organic-poor rocks. Black-shale-preserved carbonaceous compressions have become more common since the Ediacaran Period. To explore the depositional context of carbonaceous compressions, micro X-ray fluorescence spectroscopy (μ-XRF) was used to image elemental distributions in carbonaceous compressions and surrounding rocks in Mesoproterozoic and Ediacaran-aged rocks. The carbonaceous compressions preserved in the Xiamaling green silty mudstones (1.40 Ga) and Lantian black shales (0.63 Ga) were selected and scanned, respectively. The behavior of redox-sensitive elements (Mo, U, V, Zn, Cu) in the Xiamaling and Lantian rocks and carbonaceous compressions suggest that the overlying water conditions during their sedimentation were not sulfidic. However, the co-enrichments of Fe and S in Xiamaling and Lantian carbonaceous compressions indicate pyrite permineralization. The Lantian carbonaceous compressions have a higher pyrite permineralization degree and a lower organism decomposition degree than those of the Xiamaling carbonaceous compressions. We speculate that these differences are related to a higher sulfate reduction rate and a lower dissimilatory iron reduction rate in the sediments hosting the Lantian carbonaceous compressions. Such conditions might be achieved through rapid burial and encircling by clay minerals. Overall, our results shed new light on understanding the preservation processes of the Precambrian life and the influence of environmental factors.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Zhang, Fenglian","Wang, Huajian","Ye, Yuntao","Deng, Yan","Lyu, Yitong","Wang, Xiaomei","Yu, Zhichao","Lyu, Dan","Lu, Yuanzheng","Zhou, Chuanming","Bi, Lina","Deng, Shenghui","Zhang, Shuichang","Canfield, Donald E."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-598718"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Wang, Huajian"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","China National Petroleum Corporation","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Peking University"],"keyword":["XRF","Xiamaling Formation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the environmental context of carbonaceous compressions and implications for organism preservation 000000000001 000000000040 ga and 000000000000 000000000063 ga","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85105705916","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank Dr. Chengguo Guan from the Nanjing Institute of Geology and Palaeonotology, and Dr. Xiaoqi Wang, Hang Jiao from Research Institute of Petroleum Exploration and Development for their advice during the experiments. The research is financially supported by the National Key Research and Development Program of China ( 2017YFC0603101 ), the National Natural Science Foundation of China ( 41872125 , 41530317 ), Strategic Priority Research Program of the Chinese Academy of Sciences ( XDA14010101 ), National Science and Technology Major Project of the Ministry of Science and Technology of China ( 2016ZX05004001 ), and the DEC acknowledges support from the Villum Foundation of Denmark (grant 16518 )."],"id":"S01-000.00-598718","identifier":[{"id":"85105705916","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-58fa4b8f-c62b-40fe-b6ef-7f8f2fce71f4"],"keyword":["Fossil preservation","Lantian Formation","Multi-element imaging","Xiamaling Formation","μ-XRF"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7BEE4E2F310818C047876BA05AEB3DDB"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"china national petroleum corporation","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China National Petroleum Corporation","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"peking university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Peking University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Danish Institute for Advanced Study","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Nordcee"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fenglian","key":"zhangfenglianpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Fenglian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Huajian","key":"wanghuajianpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Huajian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuntao","key":"yeyuntaopau","last":"Ye","name":"Ye, Yuntao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yan","key":"dengyanpau","last":"Deng","name":"Deng, Yan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yitong","key":"lyuyitongpau","last":"Lyu","name":"Lyu, Yitong","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaomei","key":"wangxiaomeipau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xiaomei","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhichao","key":"yuzhichaopau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Zhichao","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan","key":"lyudanpau","last":"Lyu","name":"Lyu, Dan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuanzheng","key":"luyuanzhengpau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Yuanzheng","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Chuanming","key":"zhouchuanmingpau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Chuanming","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lina","key":"bilinapau","last":"Bi","name":"Bi, Lina","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shenghui","key":"dengshenghuipau","last":"Deng","name":"Deng, Shenghui","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuichang","key":"zhangshuichangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Shuichang","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Donald E.","key":"canfielddonaldepau","last":"Canfield","locid":"916eabe6-766d-4018-a5b0-3695497582bb","name":"Canfield, Donald E.","orcid":"0000-0001-7602-8366","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.palaeo.2021.110449","issn":["00310182"],"journal":"Palaeogeography, Palaeoclimatology, Palaeoecology","paperid":"110449","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Palaeogeography, Palaeoclimatology, Palaeoecology","volume":"573"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85105705916"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-58fa4b8f-c62b-40fe-b6ef-7f8f2fce71f4"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The environmental context of carbonaceous compressions and implications for organism preservation 1.40 Ga and 0.63 Ga","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-598718","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Appropriate air supply system controller is of great significance to improve the performance of proton exchange membrane fuel cell. Most of controllers rely on the high-precision, simple, and interpretable model. It is particularly important to establish the model for the fuel cell air supply system. Since the high-precision physically interpretable control-oriented model can provide an understanding of the underlying phenomena apart from computational tractability for aerodynamic problems. Data-driven sparse identification based on auto-encoder method is proposed to establish the model. It can be divided into the four steps. Firstly, collect data from a simulation model and the actual fuel cell system, and auto-encoder network is used to discover a coordinate transformation into a reduced space. Secondly, dictionary library is constructed from candidate terms based on system analysis. Thirdly, air supply model reconstruction problem is transformed into a sparse identification problem. Finally, the developed model is verified by two datasets. Compared with other methods, the results show that mean absolute error and root mean squared error of the three variables for proposed method are the smallest under both simulation data and real data. And the reconstruction results perfectly agree with the original simulation and the real data. Especially, the proposed method can be easily extended to other system modeling studies, such as the hydrogen supply system model and thermal management system model of the fuel cell system.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Deng, Zhihua","Chen, Qihong","Zhang, Liyan","Zhou, Keliang","Zong, Yi","Fu, Zhichao","Liu, Hao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-325041"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Chen, Qihong"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Wuhan University of Technology","Zhejiang University"],"keyword":["Proton exchange membrane fuel cell"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"data driven reconstruction of interpretable model for air supply system of proton exchange membrane fuel cell","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85108560603","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors would like to thank the support of the National Key Research and Development Program of China (2019YFB1504703), the Fundamental Research Funds for the Central Universities (2020YB034), and China Scholarship Council (202006950031). This work is also supported by the “SPGC” (640170582) and “PRESS” (807300026B) projects granted by the Danish Energy Technology Development and Demonstration program (EUDP) and the Danish Agency for Science & Higher Education, respectively. The anonymous reviewers’ insightful comments and valuable suggestions are also greatly appreciated."],"id":"S01-000.00-325041","identifier":[{"id":"85108560603","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-44d52be4-5baa-48d4-baba-4a78123c55ec"],"keyword":["Air supply system","Auto-encoder network","Model reconstruction","Proton exchange membrane fuel cell","Sparse identification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-78DB30B2A3774FEEF8F3DF8D83A3E6D2"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"wuhan university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Wuhan University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Electric Power and Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Electric Power and Energy, Distributed Energy Resources","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhihua","key":"dengpau","last":"Deng","name":"Deng, Zhihua","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qihong","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Qihong","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Liyan","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Liyan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Keliang","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Keliang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi","key":"zongpau","last":"Zong","locid":"3063028d-1dc8-4394-8afb-e1b09eb39672","name":"Zong, Yi","orcid":"0000-0003-1262-3558","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhichao","key":"fupau","last":"Fu","name":"Fu, Zhichao","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hao","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Hao","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.apenergy.2021.117266","issn":["03062619","18729118"],"issn_org":["03062619"],"journal":"Applied Energy","paperid":"117266","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Applied Energy","volume":"299"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85108560603"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-44d52be4-5baa-48d4-baba-4a78123c55ec"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Data-driven reconstruction of interpretable model for air supply system of proton exchange membrane fuel cell","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-325041","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Although extrachromosomal DNA (ecDNA) has been intensively studied for several decades, the mechanisms underlying its tumorigenic effects have been revealed only recently. In most conventional sequencing studies, the high-throughput short-read sequencing largely ignores the epigenetic status of most ecDNA regions except for the junctional areas. Methods: Here, we developed a method of sequencing enzyme-accessible chromatin in circular DNA (CCDA-seq) based on the use of methylase to label open chromatin without fragmentation and exonuclease to enrich ecDNA sequencing depth, followed by long-read nanopore sequencing. Results: Using CCDA-seq, we observed significantly different patterns in nucleosome/regulator binding to ecDNA at a single-molecule resolution. Conclusions: These results deepen the understanding of ecDNA regulatory mechanisms.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Chen, Weitian","Weng, Zhe","Xie, Zhe","Xie, Yeming","Zhang, Chen","Chen, Zhichao","Ruan, Fengying","Wang, Juan","Sun, Yuxin","Fang, Yitong","Guo, Mei","Tong, Yiqin","Li, Yaning","Tang, Chong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-453848"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","Beihua University","Nantong University","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Chromatin accessibility","Methylation","Methyltransferase","ecDNA","mA"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sequencing of methylase accessible regions in integral circular extrachromosomal dna reveals differences in chromatin structure","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13072-021-00416-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-453848","identifier":[{"id":"34425889","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85113777682","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8383416","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-6519e97c-4cff-44a6-bf7a-23db99c3f6be"],"keyword":["Chromatin accessibility","Methylation","Methyltransferase","ecDNA","mA"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-98E01847CCEB4F31505607CFA4F25603"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/279119761/Sequencing_of_methylase_accessible_regions_in_integral_circular_extrachromosomal_DNA_reveals_differences_in_chromatin_structure.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13072-021-00416-5","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"bgi","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Cell Biology and Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"nantong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nantong University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"beihua university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Beihua University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Weitian","key":"chenweitianpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Weitian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","