of methylase-accessible regions in integral circular extrachromosomal DNA reveals differences in chromatin structure","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-453848","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Bcl-2 and Mcl-1, the two arms of the anti-apoptotic Bcl-2 family proteins, have been identified as key regulators of apoptosis and effective therapeutic targets of cancer. However, no small molecular probe is capable of profiling and visualizing both Bcl-2 and Mcl-1 simultaneously in situ . Herein, we reported a multi-functional molecular probe ( BnN 3 -OPD-Alk ) by a \"three-in-one\" molecular designing strategy, which integrated the Bcl-2/Mcl-1 binding ligand, fluorescent reporter group and photoreactive group azido into the same scaffold. BnN 3 -OPD-Alk exhibited sub-μM affinities to Bcl-2/Mcl-1 and bright green self-fluorescence. It was then successfully applied for Bcl-2/Mcl-1 labelling, capturing, enriching, and bioimaging both in vitro and in cells. This strategy could facilitate the precise early diagnosis and effective therapy of dual Bcl-2/Mcl-1-related diseases.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Zhang, Xiaodong","Wang, Ziqian","Guo, Zongwei","Song, Ting","He, Nianzhe","Zhu, Junjie","Cao, Keke","Zhang, Zhichao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-380565"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Zhang, Zhichao"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Dalian University of Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a three in one multi functional probe for bcl 000000000002 mcl 000000000001 profiling and visualizing in situ","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/219902919/ANSA_cbic.202000441.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-380565","identifier":[{"id":"32881291","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85092557770","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-fdf5663a-972d-4f90-8365-a2d2e901baf5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6A63DD1886B11418CDB6FB3895E96ABE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/219902919/ANSA_cbic.202000441.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"dalian university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Dalian University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaodong","key":"zhangxiaodongpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xiaodong","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ziqian","key":"wangziqianpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Ziqian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zongwei","key":"guozongweipau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Zongwei","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ting","key":"songtingpau","last":"Song","name":"Song, Ting","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nianzhe","key":"henianzhepau","last":"He","locid":"cee0aa46-6034-4ff1-a945-18a68e3f2891","name":"He, Nianzhe","orcid":"0000-0003-1871-3896","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Junjie","key":"zhujunjiepau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Junjie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Keke","key":"caokekepau","last":"Cao","name":"Cao, Keke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhichao","key":"zhangzhichaopau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Zhichao","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32881291"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/cbic.202000441","issn":["14394227","14397633"],"issn_org":["14394227"],"issue":"2","journal":"ChemBioChem","pages":"326-329","publisher":"Wiley - VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA","publisher_org":"Wiley - V C H Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA","status":"p","title":"ChemBioChem","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85092557770"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-fdf5663a-972d-4f90-8365-a2d2e901baf5"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A \"three-in-one\" multi-functional probe for Bcl-2/Mcl-1 profiling and visualizing in situ","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-380565","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Proton exchange membrane fuel cell systems are widely used to drive vehicles. It is indispensable to establish accurate and simple control oriented model of the system. However, this control oriented model is difficult to build due to the characteristic of strongly nonlinear, coupled and time - varying in proton exchange membrane fuel cell systems. To solve this problem, nonlinear subspace identification method is proposed to discover linear parameter varying model for the proton exchange membrane fuel cell system. The modeling process can be divided into two stages. In the first stage, algebraic transformation method is proposed to transform the nonlinear model to linear parameter varying model. In the second stage, kernel method based subspace identification is presented to identify parameter matrices of the proton exchange membrane fuel cell system. The established model is demonstrated by a 50 kW on board proton exchange membrane fuel cell system under real driving condition. The results show that mean absolute percent error and root mean squared error are as low as 9.6941e−06 and 0.0957, respectively. Therefore, the control oriented model perfectly agrees with real data. Compared with the prediction error method and recursive neural network nonlinear auto - regressive moving average model with exogenous method, modeling accuracy and speed of the proposed method are the best. Moreover, linear control theory can be employed to design controller based on the linear parameter varying model, which greatly simplifies controller design for proton exchange membrane fuel cell systems.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Deng, Zhihua","Chen, Qihong","Zhang, Liyan","Zong, Yi","Zhou, Keliang","Fu, Zhichao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-306367"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Chen, Qihong"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Wuhan University of Technology"],"keyword":["Data driven modeling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"control oriented data driven linear parameter varying model for proton exchange membrane fuel cell systems","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85088827609","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors would like to thank the support of National Natural Science Foundation of China under grant 61673306, 61673305, National Key Research and Development Program of China under grant 2019YFB1504703, and the project granted by the Danish Agency for Science and Higher Education (No. 8073-00026B). This work is also supported by ”the Fundamental Research Funds for the Central Universities” under grant 2020-YB-034."],"id":"S01-000.00-306367","identifier":[{"id":"85088827609","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-05f2cadf-3dbb-40d0-80b8-0213729f729b"],"keyword":["Data driven modeling","Kernel method","Linear parameter varying system","Nonlinear subspace identification method","Proton exchange membrane fuel cell system"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-230D40E5D105A2C519D9653F120D1660"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"wuhan university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Wuhan University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Electric Power and Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Electric Power and Energy, Distributed Energy Resources","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhihua","key":"dengpau","last":"Deng","name":"Deng, Zhihua","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qihong","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Qihong","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Liyan","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Liyan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi","key":"zongpau","last":"Zong","locid":"3063028d-1dc8-4394-8afb-e1b09eb39672","name":"Zong, Yi","orcid":"0000-0003-1262-3558","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Keliang","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Keliang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhichao","key":"fupau","last":"Fu","name":"Fu, Zhichao","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.apenergy.2020.115540","issn":["03062619","18729118"],"issn_org":["03062619"],"journal":"Applied Energy","paperid":"115540","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Applied Energy","volume":"277"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088827609"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-05f2cadf-3dbb-40d0-80b8-0213729f729b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Control oriented data driven linear parameter varying model for proton exchange membrane fuel cell systems","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-306367","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Repetitive control (RC) presents an attractive solution to achieve low steady-state tracking error and total harmonic distortion (THD) for periodic signals. For conventional RC (CRC), it requires that the ratio of reference signal period to the fixed sampling period to be an integer. Therefore, the reference signal with variable frequency or a fractional period ratio will lead to severe performance degradation. Although existing hardware variable sampling rate methods enable CRC to be frequency adaptive, the variable sampling frequency will also influence the overall system stability, and they need that the CPU has variable sampling frequency ability. In this paper, a flexible and easy-to-implement method, virtual variable sampling (VVS), is proposed to enable RC to be frequency adaptive. The proposed VVS method, which creates a virtual delay unit to approximate each variable sampling delay, achieves a flexible variable sampling as similar as hardwarebased variable sampling, but it does not influence overall system sampling frequency and stability. Experimental results of a single phase DC/AC converter system are presented to show the effectiveness of the proposed VVS-RC.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Liu, Zhichao","Zhang, Bin","Zhou, Keliang","Yang, Yongheng","Wang, Jingcheng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-083007"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["China","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Shanghai Jiao Tong University","University of Glasgow","University of South Carolina"],"keyword":["DC AC converter","Repetitive control RC","Total harmonic distortion THD"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"virtual variable sampling repetitive control of single phase dc ac pwm converters","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/283994290/08424335.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-083007","identifier":[{"id":"000478946200042","type":"wos"},{"id":"85050989011","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-713c404d-c42e-4dd2-bff1-ed7c4ff77403"],"keyword":["DC/AC converter","Fractional delay length","Phase lead compensation","Repetitive control (RC)","Total harmonic distortion (THD)","Virtual variable sampling (VVS)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1D1C69C5172925DA40FEABA7384D4508"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/283994290/08424335.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of south carolina","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of South Carolina","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of glasgow","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Glasgow","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"shanghai jiao tong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhichao","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Zhichao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bin","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Bin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Keliang","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Keliang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yongheng","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","locid":"d4e88c1b-191c-43c1-90e4-13e51951780e","name":"Yang, Yongheng","orcid":"0000-0002-1488-4762","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jingcheng","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Jingcheng","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/jestpe.2018.2862411","issn":["21686777","21686785"],"issn_org":["21686777"],"issue":"3","journal":"IEEE Journal of Emerging and Selected Topics in Power Electronics","pages":"1837-1845","paperid":"8424335","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Journal of Emerging and Selected Topics in Power Electronics","title_org":"I E E E Journal of Emerging and Selected Topics in Power Electronics","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85050989011"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-713c404d-c42e-4dd2-bff1-ed7c4ff77403"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Virtual Variable Sampling Repetitive Control of Single-phase DC/AC PWM Converters","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-083007","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Life cycle assessment (LCA) is a useful tool for quantifying the overall environmental impacts of a product, process, or service. The scientific scope and boundary definition are important to ensure the accuracy of LCA results. Defining the boundary in LCA is difficult and there are no commonly accepted scientific methods yet. The objective of this research is to present a comprehensive discussion of system boundaries in LCA and to develop an appropriate boundary delimitation method.A product system is partitioned into the primary system and interrelated subsystems. The hierarchical relationship of flow and process is clarified by introducing flow- and process-related interventions. A system boundary curve model of the LCA is developed and the threshold rules for judging whether the system boundary satisfies the research requirement are proposed. Quantitative criteria from environmental, technical, geographical and temporal dimensions are presented to limit the boundaries of LCA. An algorithm is developed to identify an appropriate boundary by searching the process tree and evaluating the environmental impact contribution of each process while it is added into the studied system.The difference between a limited system and a theoretically complete system is presented. A case study is conducted on a color TV set to demonstrate and validate the method of boundary identification. The results showed that the overall environmental impact indicator exhibits a slow growth after a certain number of processes considered, and the gradient of the fitting curve trends to zero gradually. According to the threshold rules, a relatively accurate system boundary could be obtained.It is found from this research that the system boundary curve describes the growth of life cycle impact assessment (LCIA) results as processes are added. The two threshold rules and identification methods presented can be used to identify system boundary of LCA. The case study demonstrated that the methodology presented in this paper is an effective tool for the boundary identification.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Li, Tao","Zhang, Hongchao","Liu, Zhichao","Ke, Qingdi","Alting, Leo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-327423"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Dalian University of Technology","Hefei University of Technology"],"keyword":["Life cycle assessment","Search algorithm"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a system boundary identification method for life cycle assessment","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11367-013-0654-5","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-327423","identifier":[{"id":"84898876625","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-4cc5104f-21b0-4916-9b07-952375bbfd08"],"keyword":["Life cycle assessment","Process tree","Search algorithm","System boundary","Threshold rule"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-50527D46B6D5E0127A40682BF855FA8E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11367-013-0654-5","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"dalian university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Dalian University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"hefei university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hefei University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Te